[h1]Phobos Shipbreaker[/h1]
[h2]Powered G4 reclamation in 0.24.0[/h2]
Explicitly start one bound G4/H4/D4 mission: capture a supported ordinary wall, cut/feed, release, retreat, traverse outside the collision boundary and recapture. Existing equipment, artwork and manual 2 kW transfer remain. Requires Auto Nav 0.18.0 with N1/N2 and Framework 0.24.0.
Authored cutter defaults are 120 powered seconds at 12 kW, credited from actual electricity. Heat enters the connected D4 service room, requiring 10 kPa and a 40 C ceiling. This cooling connection is a gameplay abstraction; vacuum supplies no free cooling. Cutting and transfer are sequential.
Only exposed, undamaged, empty, unstacked native 24 kg ordinary walls on an owned, unoccupied, depressurized target qualify. Floors, protected anchor supports, other equipment and target registration remain. Separate native uninstall/transfer journals preserve exact physical identity and paid work. Uncertain mutation suspends; missing cargo is never reconstructed.
Local G4, C1 and F3 provide Start, Resume, Pause, Stop and status. Full capacity waits while the same mission stays authorized. Manual movement, contact loss and loading suspend authority; Stop retains capture and Release is explicit. Older captures need a new protected-support plan before cutting. No whole-wreck deletion, new structural recipes or repeated furnace batches. Existing furnace motion restrictions remain. Prepared offline; gameplay evaluation and publication are pending.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/shipbreaker-reclamation.md]Reclamation setup, cooling, limits and recovery[/url]

[h2]Selected-G4 capture in 0.22.0[/h2]
Bind one G4, its chute/D4 and an existing N1/N2 console/module to a selected owned, unoccupied target. Auto Nav approaches with exclusive propulsion control; separate native mooring anchors establish deck contact after a fit check. Local industrial panels, C1 and F3 offer Bind, Start/Resume, Stop and Release. Full saved IDs survive reload; live permission does not. Stop/release do not brake. All target cargo remains intact.
The 0.24.0 reclamation extension above adds bounded cutting and repositioning. Repeated furnace cycles and whole-wreck completion remain excluded. Prepared offline; gameplay evaluation and publication remain pending.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/shipbreaker-capture.md]Capture controls, native evidence and limits[/url]
[h2]Solar-system economy in 0.21.0[/h2]
Industrial equipment, assembly sections, coolant conduits and finite coolant charges gain bounded offers at 15 additional placed vanilla retail markets. Industrial centres receive higher authored availability; Flotilla machinery is refurbished. Clean coolant now uses the industrial category and retained coolant uses trash, never potable water. Base values, material budgets and jobs are preserved.
Requires Phobos Framework 0.23.0 or newer. Authored availability follows native economic roles; native supply/demand, merchant terms and restocking remain in control. No new settlements, guaranteed stock or live-price promises. Prepared offline, not gameplay-validated or published.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/solar-system-economy.md]Regional coverage, sources and limits[/url]
[h2]Pending-construction room-load mitigation in 0.19.1[/h2]
The grid guard introduced with Framework 0.21.1 restores checked saved bounds before native room/zone assignments when pending Shipbreaker equipment reduces the loading grid. Update to Framework 0.24.1 for both follow-ups: preserve living worn markers and correct stale dimensions captured before native save trimming. The grid guard previously trusted that stale header. Damage, construction progress and recorded atmosphere are preserved; gas already lost cannot be recreated. The first two owner-tested fixes worked on their reported saves; gameplay confirmation of the third is pending.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/shipbreaker-room-load-mitigation.md]Evidence, limits and reload check[/url]
[h2]Shared completion cues in 0.19.0[/h2]
Requires Phobos Framework 0.22.0 or newer. D4/R4 watches now use the shared Phobos volume/mute and one audio channel across mods. Existing one-batch meaning and original sound remain; no new furnace, transfer or ambient cues. Gameplay/listening review pending.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/shared-completion-cues.md]Shared controls and limits[/url]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.24.1
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - development candidate

Recover useful shipbuilding materials and manage onboard industry with Phobos' Rivetline equipment and the Phobos' Asterel C1 Industrial Control Console.

[h2]Current features[/h2]
[list]
[*]Process manually supplied detached wall panels; connect a grabber, wall chute and indoor dismantling fixture.
[*]Recover steel and aluminium from identified processing residue, retaining finite rejects.
[*]Pair collectors and material routes explicitly; manage machines through local Control Panels, C1 or F3.
[*]Optionally watch one D4/R4 batch: a brief quiet tone and visible status confirm products committed to its output tray. Volume/mute follows native sound-effects volume; further queued batches stay silent.
[*]Cast aluminium housings with the electrically heated F6 furnace and finite cooling.
[*]Choose existing direct exterior or underside cooling, or optional F6-C sealed conduits to a remote F6-R radiator.
[*]INSTALL catalogue: APPS for D4, grabber, chute, collector, R4 and F6; HVAC for F6-R, F6-P and F6-C; CTRL for C1. Intact and damaged forms retain normal physical installation requirements. Prepared; gameplay review pending.
[/list]

[h2]Limits and save behaviour[/h2]
[list]
[*]Experimental candidate; current machinery and artwork still need in-game evaluation.
[*]Attached cutting is restricted to supported ordinary walls. No persistent cargo ejection or perfect recycling. Recipe yields are authored gameplay budgets.
[*]Processing and receiving are separate permissions and pause after reload. Saved links are retained.
[*]Completion watches are session-only and clear on processing Pause/Cancel, fault or reload. Audio is restricted to the requesting selected crew on the same ship. Muted or suppressed events are never replayed. Listening evaluation is pending; no guaranteed native alarm suppression.
[*]Cooling uses a simplified thermal model with optional finite coolant servicing. Direct coupling can transfer furnace heat without power; piped circulation requires electricity. On power loss, the radiator still rejects its own stored heat and the furnace retains bounded room leakage. Piped circulation adds up to 1 kW; cold feed motors use 2 kW by default. Existing direct and legacy sealed installations retain their saved meaning.
[/list]

[h2]Original trial in 0.18.0[/h2]
First optional watched-batch audio trial: one original 280 ms tone after a D4/R4 output commit, with quiet volume/mute, explicit watch/unwatch controls and no queued playback. No new furnace, navigation or ambient cues; existing material routes and saves retain their meaning. Reclaimer fallback controls now scroll.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/shipbreaker-completion-cue.md]Completion cue controls and listening checks[/url]

[h2]Requirements and installation[/h2]
Auto Nav is now mandatory. Capture uses existing N1/N2 hardware; no new navigation module or grabber identity is introduced.

Ostranauts 1.0.1.5, BepInEx 5 and Phobos Framework 0.24.0+ and Phobos Auto Nav 0.16.0+. Agriculture remains optional. No Crafting Framework or Salvage Workshop dependency.

This is a maintained pre-publication page draft, not a download announcement. No Workshop item has been published for this draft. Use the installation guide for source/prepared-package availability and loader setup. Do not remove required providers from saves that contain their content.

