[h2]Nutrient recovery and optional wet-reject collection[/h2]
Requires Framework 0.24.2 for shared panel feedback. Collector routing and local/C1 furnace controls suppress successful status echoes while retaining rejection explanations and distinct notices. Furnace readouts refresh immediately after instrument actions.
Optional Agriculture integration reuses the original Residue Collector with finite capacity and exclusive pairing. Shipbreaker 0.24.1 permits floor mounting on two structural tiles with a clear two-tile service walkway, while retaining existing hull-mount support rules. Agriculture 0.11.1 aligns its complete pocket edge against the Recycler, including directly in front; its service side faces away. Saved links and cargo remain intact; misaligned pairs wait for correction or explicit Unlink. Framework 0.22.0 and Shipbreaker 0.20.0 introduced measured wet-reject capture from [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3757331189]Valtora’s Ship’s Water 0.16.1[/url]. Full or unavailable linked collectors hold wastewater in its source tank. No wastewater-to-fertilizer recipe is claimed. Prepared offline; gameplay confirmation pending. [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/agriculture-nutrient-production.md]Operating guide, economic limits and research attribution[/url].

[h2]Bulk merchant stock[/h2]
Increase successful local and regional offers to wholesale lots for all machinery, assembly sections, coolant conduit and service charges. Uses Framework 0.24.0; prices, engineering salvage and existing inventories are unchanged.
Normal restocking is required; updating does not refill existing shops. [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/merchant-stock.md]Current quantities and restocking guide[/url]. Prepared candidate; in-game stock/capacity review pending.
